  "body": "<p>Coco Gauff has typically had her way against younger players, and that trend continued Monday night in Beijing, though not without a fight. The World No. 4 pulled away late, winning nine of the final 10 games to beat 16-year-old <a href=\"https://www.wtatennis.com/players/335958/xinran-sun\">Sun Xinran</a> 7-5, 6-1 in 1 hour, 29 minutes and advance to the Round of 16 for the fourth consecutive year.</p>\n<p><strong><em>Beijing: <a href=\"https://www.wtatennis.com/tournaments/china-open/scores\" data-tracking=\"true\" data-tracking-event=\"click_track\" data-tracking-component=\"link click\" data-tracking-category=\"content\" data-tracking-type=\"news\" data-tracking-detail=\"Scores\" data-tracking-widget-type=\"Article Widget\" data-tracking-widget-name=\"Article Page Widget\">Scores</a> | <a href=\"https://www.wtatennis.com/tournaments/china-open/order-of-play\" data-tracking=\"true\" data-tracking-event=\"click_track\" data-tracking-component=\"link click\" data-tracking-category=\"content\" data-tracking-type=\"news\" data-tracking-detail=\"Order of play\" data-tracking-widget-type=\"Article Widget\" data-tracking-widget-name=\"Article Page Widget\">Order of play</a> | <a href=\"https://www.wtatennis.com/tournaments/china-open/draws\" data-tracking=\"true\" data-tracking-event=\"click_track\" data-tracking-component=\"link click\" data-tracking-category=\"content\" data-tracking-type=\"news\" data-tracking-detail=\"Draws\" data-tracking-widget-type=\"Article Widget\" data-tracking-widget-name=\"Article Page Widget\">Draws</a></em></strong></p>\n<p>Gauff has now won 24 of her 28 career matches at the WTA Tour Driven by Mercedes-Benz level against opponents younger. Her only loss to a teenager during that span came against eventual champion Victoria Mboko in Montreal in 2025.</p>\n<div id=\"\" class=\"twitterThumb center\" title=\"Embedded Tweet\" contenteditable=\"false\">\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet\">\n<p dir=\"ltr\" lang=\"en\">Returning to the Round of 16 💪 @CocoGauff moves past Sun in straight sets and continues to push towards a place at WTA Finals Indian Wells! #ChinaOpen https://t.co/Ksy9n9xbLI</p>\n— wta (@WTA) <a href=\"https://x.com/WTA/status/2107134785386660043?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw\">October 5, 2026</a></blockquote>\n</div>\n<p>Despite the result, Gauff had nothing but praise for the young Chinese standout.</p>\n<p>\"I think she's a little bit more mature than I was at 16,\" Gauff said in her post-match interview. \"I think I got a little bit more frustrated than she did. But she's an incredible player. I knew going in it was going to be a tough match. The junior career that she's had is incredible, and obviously she's going to do great at this level.</p>\n<p>\"I think this is the first of many matches on this court and many matches that we will play against each other. I'm looking forward to the future matchups we have.\"</p>\n<p><em>More to come...</em></p><script async src=\"//platform.twitter.com/widgets.js\"></script>",
